---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" interior>
  <article class="article">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Hello! I'm Adrianne.</h1>
    <p>I'm a staff software engineer based in Portland, Oregon. My pronouns are they/them. I build design systems and frontend infrastructure, and I care about making complex software easier to use and maintain.</p>
    <p><a href="mailto:me@adriannedaley.com">Get in touch</a> or <a href="/resume/">read my full resume</a>.</p>

    <h2>A little work history</h2>
    <h3><a href="https://www.honeycomb.io/">Honeycomb</a></h3>
    <p class="meta">Staff Software Engineer · <time datetime="2024">2024</time>–present</p>
    <p>I lead the Design Enablement team, building the design system and frontend infrastructure used across Honeycomb's engineering organization.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.hashicorp.com/">HashiCorp</a></h3>
    <p class="meta">Senior and Staff Software Engineer · <time datetime="2018">2018</time>–<time datetime="2024">2024</time></p>
    <p>I founded and led the <a href="https://www.hashicorp.com/en/products/vault/hcp-vault-dedicated">HCP Vault</a> UI team, taking the product from inception to general availability. Before that, I built Vault's first data visualization and its JavaScript component library.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://newrelic.com/">New Relic</a></h3>
    <p class="meta">Software Engineer I–III · <time datetime="2014">2014</time>–<time datetime="2018">2018</time></p>
    <p>I worked on APM's Error Analytics and reusable React components, and led the rebuild of an internal Rails application. I also co-led an internal UI education group.</p>

    <h2>Before software</h2>
    <p>I studied sociology at UC Santa Cruz and software engineering at Hackbright Academy. My earlier work in community management still shapes how I approach software. Understanding people matters as much as understanding the code.</p>
    <p>I'm interested in building a more empathetic, human-centered tech industry. I share writing and talks about that, design, and software on my <a href="/posts/">blog</a>.</p>

    <h2>Away from the keyboard</h2>
    <p>You'll find me organizing community bike rides, reading nonfiction, or scheming up my next big <a href="https://drive.google.com/open?id=1muxaKlQ9ndnV7dptPwHesS8o89w&usp=sharing">travel adventure</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
